{title: Joy to the World - rev. 10-27-2026}
{subtitle: Isaac Watts, 1719}
{define D7 frets 2 2 2 3}
{comment: Tempo: 90 / Strum: d- du du du} 

{comment: Strum in on [*[G]]}

{comment: Verse 1:}
[G] Joy to the world, the [D] Lord is [G] come!  
Let [C] earth re-[D]ceive her [G] King;
Let [G] every heart pre-[G]pare Him room,
And [G] Heaven and nature sing,
And [D] Heaven and nature [D7] sing,
And [G] Heaven, and Heaven, and [D] nature [G] sing. [G] 

{comment: Verse 2:}
[G] Joy to the earth, the [D] Savior [G] reigns!
Let [C] all their [D] songs em-[G]ploy;
[G] While fields and floods, rocks, [G] hills and plains
Re-[G]peat the sounding joy,
Re-[D]peat the sounding [D7] joy,
Re-[G]peat, repeat, the [D] sounding [G] joy. [G] 

{comment: Verse 2:}
[G] He rules the world with truth [D] and [G] grace,
And [C] makes the [D] nations [G] prove
The [G] glories of His [G] righteousness,
And [G] wonders of His love,
And [D] wonders of His [D7] love,
And [G] wonders, wonders, [D] of His [G] [*/(hold)] love. 
 
